 > Rumor has it the cat is always dead....how 'bout programming in this sequence
 > of output:
 > 
 > The Schroedinger's cat gets out of the box!
 > The Schroedinger's cat is dead! -more-
 > The Schroedinger's cat is alive! 
 > The Schroedinger's cat is both! -more-
 > You are confused....
 > The Schroedinger's cat vanishes in a puff of logic. 

The cat have to be either alive or dead when you OBSERVE it (i.e.
open the box.) It is just inside the box it can be 'both'.

I would rather see a possibility for small monsters to exist alive
inside a box.  This could be another type of box-trap.  

It should be possible to pick up live monsters, if they aren't too heavy.
Having an angry monster in the inventory would not be a good idea,
as it would attack you all the time, and it would break out of a bag, possibly
out of a box if strong enough.  (An ice box would do frost damage.)
Uses for this possibility would be to pick up a small monster and throw it
into a wall (extra damage), water (drowning), lava (grilling it), a trap
, another monster (damage to both), or just throw it away.  Giants and other
really strong monsters would probably enjoy tossing players around.
Another use of the pickup command would be to pick up your cat
before levitating to the other side of a moat or some such.

Tame monsters shouldn't drop everything they have.  A tame orc should
keep its armor and weapon, wands and scrolls.  An intelligent tame monster
would switch to better weapons and armor when it found something.
They could still drop items they don't need, such as extra weapons and armor,
and used-up wands.
